WEBVTT

1
00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:29.833


2
00:00:29.833 --> 00:00:32.625
<b>Arjun is expressing his disgust here.</b>

3
00:00:32.625 --> 00:00:35.791
<b>He says, what a great sin it is,</b>

4
00:00:35.791 --> 00:00:41.583
<b>that we are ready to kill our own relatives</b>
<b>out of greed for the kingdom.</b>

5
00:00:42.125 --> 00:00:46.291


6
00:00:46.291 --> 00:00:47.666
<b>Arjun says</b>

7
00:00:47.666 --> 00:00:52.291
<b>that even thinking about</b>
<b>killing one's own relatives is a crime, </b>

8
00:00:52.291 --> 00:00:57.375
<b>let alone actually doing it!</b>
<b>Arjun calls this 'mahat-paapam',</b>

9
00:00:57.375 --> 00:01:01.208
<b>meaning one of the greatest sins.</b>

10
00:01:01.208 --> 00:01:05.625
<b>Earlier, he was calling Dhritarashtra's sons</b>
<b>greedy and unrighteous,</b>

11
00:01:05.625 --> 00:01:07.625
<b>but now he's starting to feel</b>

12
00:01:07.625 --> 00:01:09.833
<b> that he himself is no different.</b>

13
00:01:09.833 --> 00:01:13.333
<b>Isn't he doing all this for the throne too?</b>

14
00:01:13.333 --> 00:01:14.000
<b>But</b>

15
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:18.083
<b>you know that Arjun isn't doing</b>
<b>all this for the throne,</b>

16
00:01:18.083 --> 00:01:19.791
<b>he's doing it for dharma.</b>

17
00:01:19.791 --> 00:01:25.666
<b>How could Lord Krishna, who is his charioteer,</b>
<b>allow him to commit any sin?</b>

18
00:01:25.666 --> 00:01:31.000
<b>However, Arjun's anguish at this</b>
<b>moment is turning into self-loathing.</b>

19
00:01:31.583 --> 00:01:35.791


20
00:01:35.791 --> 00:01:38.250
<b>Arjun's belief </b>

21
00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:43.500
<b>that even thinking about</b>
<b>killing one's relatives is a crime, </b>

22
00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:45.208
<b>this very thought shows</b>

23
00:01:45.208 --> 00:01:47.750
<b>the purity of his mind and</b>

24
00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:52.958
<b>the cleanliness of his thoughts.</b>

25
00:01:52.958 --> 00:01:54.500
<b>Humans often</b>

26
00:01:54.500 --> 00:02:00.625
<b>weigh themselves heavily</b>
<b>on the scale of goodness,</b>

27
00:02:00.625 --> 00:02:03.541
<b>thinking that it was just a bad thought,</b>

28
00:02:03.541 --> 00:02:07.208
<b>they didn't do anything wrong. </b>

29
00:02:07.208 --> 00:02:09.125
<b>You tell me,</b>

30
00:02:09.125 --> 00:02:16.666
<b>isn't the mere corruption</b>
<b>of thoughts concerning?</b>

31
00:02:16.666 --> 00:02:20.916
<b>Just as a seed sprouts into a plant,</b>

32
00:02:20.916 --> 00:02:22.791
<b>in the same way,</b>

33
00:02:22.791 --> 00:02:31.125
<b>thoughts are those seeds from which, someday, </b>
<b>somewhere, our actions sprout.</b>

34
00:02:31.125 --> 00:02:33.500
<b>Every action, good or bad,</b>

35
00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:37.958
<b>begins with thoughts.</b>

36
00:02:37.958 --> 00:02:39.291
<b>Therefore,</b>

37
00:02:39.291 --> 00:02:41.291
<b>purity of mind</b>

38
00:02:41.291 --> 00:02:45.416
<b>is supreme, even over purity of action.</b>

39
00:02:45.416 --> 00:02:47.791
<b>Keep your mind clean,</b>

40
00:02:47.791 --> 00:02:50.000
<b>and your thoughts pure.</b>

41
00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:53.458
<b>Spirituality will help you in this.</b>

42
00:02:53.458 --> 00:02:55.125
<b>This Gita</b>

43
00:02:55.125 --> 00:02:58.250
<b>will guide you in this.</b>

44
00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:02.958


45
00:03:02.958 --> 00:03:04.875
<b>Greed? </b>

46
00:03:04.875 --> 00:03:07.000
<b>What is greed?</b>

47
00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:11.958
<b>Greed is the first step towards</b>
<b>the door of unrighteousness.</b>

48
00:03:11.958 --> 00:03:14.500
<b>Greed is a poisonous snake that,</b>

49
00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:17.250
<b>if it bites a person,</b>

50
00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:25.041
<b>makes them crave to accumulate</b>
<b>far more than necessary,</b>

51
00:03:25.041 --> 00:03:28.625
<b>be it wealth or property.</b>

52
00:03:28.625 --> 00:03:32.541
<b>Slowly, this poison spreads so much</b>

53
00:03:32.541 --> 00:03:37.708
<b>that it completely destroys</b>
<b>morality and wisdom.</b>

54
00:03:37.708 --> 00:03:41.541
<b>Throughout history,</b>
<b>there are countless examples</b>

55
00:03:41.541 --> 00:03:45.041
<b>where people, in their lust for power and wealth,</b>

56
00:03:45.041 --> 00:03:52.708
<b>have sent even their own</b>
<b>relatives to their deaths.</b>

57
00:03:52.708 --> 00:03:59.875
<b>Stay alert to keep your family </b>
<b>away from this poison.</b>

58
00:03:59.875 --> 00:04:02.208
<b>The antidote to this poison</b>

59
00:04:02.208 --> 00:04:06.083
<b>is mutual love and contentment.</b>

60
00:04:06.083 --> 00:04:10.875
<b>When family members truly love each other,</b>

61
00:04:10.875 --> 00:04:16.791
<b>they find satisfaction and</b>
<b>joy in the simple moments of life.</b>

62
00:04:16.791 --> 00:04:22.750
<b>Make sure to celebrate small victories</b>
<b>of everyone in the family.</b>

63
00:04:22.750 --> 00:04:25.583
<b>Encourage each other.</b>

64
00:04:25.583 --> 00:04:27.333
<b>And yes eating together.</b>

65
00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:31.125
<b>Even eating together promotes love.</b>

66
00:04:31.125 --> 00:04:33.000
<b>There are many such ways</b>

67
00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:35.750
<b>to foster mutual love and contentment.</b>

68
00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:40.416
<b>And greed cannot enter a home</b>
<b>filled with such love.</b>

69
00:04:40.916 --> 00:04:44.958


70
00:04:44.958 --> 00:04:46.041
<b>Profit </b>

71
00:04:46.041 --> 00:04:48.125
<b>and greed,</b>

72
00:04:48.125 --> 00:04:52.583
<b>there's only a small difference in</b>
<b>the measure between both. </b>

73
00:04:52.583 --> 00:04:57.791
<b>And often, humans forget this difference, </b>

74
00:04:57.791 --> 00:04:59.875
<b>just to see their profits grow,</b>

75
00:04:59.875 --> 00:05:07.500
<b>they won’t hesitate to exploit and</b>
<b>misuse those dependent on them.</b>

76
00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:13.500
<b>Exploiting a person dependent on you is a sin.</b>

77
00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:15.333
<b>There's no evil in profit;</b>

78
00:05:15.333 --> 00:05:20.625
<b>it's an important goal for any organization. </b>

79
00:05:20.625 --> 00:05:27.125
<b>But profit earned through someone else's</b>
<b>oppression never bears fruit.</b>

80
00:05:27.125 --> 00:05:29.000
<b>Know this truth.</b>

